WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.600
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day!

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.770
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.900
Hi there!

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.660
I'm a Four Star Academy first-year, Nijino Yume!

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.200
Sakuraba Rola here.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.910
And Kasumi Mahiru.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.120
With Saotome Ako.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:27.250
Today's Fresh Idol Gathering is brought to you by...{I can't help but think there's a better word than gathering for daishuugou}

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.340
The four of us!

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.720
If you miss it, I won't forgive you! {and will suck your blood}

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.470
All those who harbor passionate emotions...

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.680
Don't touch—

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.100
That dial!

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:20.570
Let's make the best of our first show together in a while!

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:25.580
Here we go!

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.830
All together!

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.830
Aikatsu!

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.300
Good job!

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:13.850
That was so much fun!

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.270
And the crowd loved it too.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:15.980
Yeah.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:18.520
It turned out to be a fantastic show.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:26.030
I got Glitter!

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:29.030
And it looks like more than usual too.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.780
I got some too!

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.620
As did I.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:36.040
Looks like we all did.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:39.540
Guess it's proof of how great our performance was.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:40.370
Yeah.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.250
I'm coming in.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:45.170
How's it going, babies?

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:46.960
Good afternoon.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.180
You deserve props for that show.

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:50.930
Thank you!

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:53.970
Now head on over to see the headmaster.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.810
I have only one thing to say.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:06.320
Starting tomorrow, you'll be off for three days.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:11.530
You've had a hectic schedule ever since day one.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.410
Take this chance to rest up.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:19.080
That said, act in accordance with what is expected of you as idols.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.250
We will.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:21.670
M-Me too!

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.300
So hey, what's this "off" thing?

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.720
Is it like switching yourself off? {not totally wrong}

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.970
Are you being serious?

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.720
Don't make me laugh.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.310
Huh? Do you know what it means, Mahiru-chan?

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:40.890
What's there to know? It means we're on break. {or vacation}

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.350
Oh, so that's it.

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:47.860
Off, huh? I like how celebrity it sounds.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:48.900
Hey everyone.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:50.900
Good job out there.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:52.610
Koharu-chan!

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:57.870
Hey, listen to this! We just got off-time! {I checked back to ep 24, they used the full term back then}

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.620
Three days starting tomorrow!

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:03.750
Really? I was given a break too.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.250
My dad's coming home for the first time in a while.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:09.260
He is? That's great, Koharu-chan.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:10.590
Yeah.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:11.920
Your father?

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:17.180
Oh, Koharu-chan's dad is away on work a lot, so they don't see each other very much.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:22.100
If she's going home, then maybe I should too.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:27.190
Will you? Could I stop by on the way home for some pastries then? {I don't normally use it, but isn't this perfect?}{it's not perfect but it's fine}

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.440
Of course!

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.440
Pastries?

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:35.110
Yume-chan's family runs a pastry shop called Rainbow Confectionery. {do you like this? opinions?}{maybe "the rainbow confectionery"}

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:37.620
I wouldn't have guessed.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:39.660
A pastry shop...

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.840
Is your Rainbow Confectionery <i>the</i> Rainbow Confectionery?

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:56.430
The Rainbow Confectionery famous for their chocolate brownies as rich as ganache?

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:58.970
Please allow me to accompany you!

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:01.680
Then I'll come too!

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:05.980
Got it. So...

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:10.110
Want to meet at the main gate tomorrow morning at nine?

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:11.690
Okay!

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.690
What about you, Ako-chan?

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:17.200
Come along with us.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:20.160
Wh-Why would I go?

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:23.200
Unlike you lot, I have things to do.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:27.210
That's too bad. I'll invite you some other time.

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:31.710
I haven't been over in a while.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.260
Yeah, I know.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:37.970
Rola, Mahiru-chan! Morning!

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:39.220
Morning.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:40.430
Good morning.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:45.350
Mahiru-chan, your clothes are so cute.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:46.480
Excuse me.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.270
You kept me waiting.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:53.610
Nijino Yume-san, you're five minutes late.

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:56.150
Wait, didn't you say you weren't coming?

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:58.490
This is what makes Ako who she is.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:01.740
Ako-chan is so cute.

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:06.250
Now that we're all here, let's head out!

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.250
Yeah!

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.880
So this is your house.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:14.630
It's a charming place.

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:18.930
I'm back!

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.390
Yume-chan! Welcome home.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:23.180
Thank you for having us.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:26.020
My, just look at all the cute girls.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.020
And it's so nice to see you again, Koharu-chan.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:29.270
Honey!

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:32.270
Hey, come on in, everyone.

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:37.530
These are my Aikatsu buddies.
Could you spare some pastries?

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:41.530
Of course. Please, make yourselves comfortable.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:44.030
They look delicious.

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:46.790
It's hard to decide where to begin.{high-stock ako-chan would never befoul her mouth with a split infinitive}

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:49.790
There's only one choice for me.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:54.550
The rainbow cream puff that's been part of the shop's specialty menu since it opened.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:59.050
Yes, this is the taste!

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:02.140
We ate a lot of them together when we were younger.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:08.060
<i>This is the chocolate brownie renowned far and wide!</i>

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.770
Forgive my transgression!

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:23.240
It's deserving of a black belt! Respect! {hmmm}

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.080
I'm glad you seem to like it.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:35.090
My tummy is full-full.{this is fine but I am surprised you this}

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:38.260
Mine too. Thanks for the treat.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:39.800
You're very welcome.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:45.720
Hey, by the way... {;_;}

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.770
Did Koharu go home?

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:51.520
Yeah, she said her dad should be getting back soon.

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:52.350
I see.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:07.370
It would be harder to talk if we all sat in a row.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:10.500
I can't stand when people are unable to read the mood.

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:12.120
This coming from you?

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.120
What of it?!

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:16.840
There she is, the Ako kitty!

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:18.130
Ako kitty?

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:25.090
I'm so glad you all came over to hang out in my room.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:29.140
Seriously, I never thought we'd all end up this close.

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:31.140
Yeah, neither did I.

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:35.150
I just got a good idea! Let's do "that" as proof of our friendship!

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:36.650
"That"?

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:41.650
Let's play pretend S4's tea party, Gathering of Stars!

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:43.650
Pretend?

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:46.660
We aren't children, you know.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:49.540
Come on, I wanna do it!

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:50.740
No thank you.

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:50.740
No way.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.410
Need I remind you...

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:57.420
That you were happily eating away at the pastries?

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.800
We are stars.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:11.060
The Four Stars that light up the Aikatsu world.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:14.310
Tirelessly serving as shining beacons in the sky.

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:17.560
Th-The radiance of our stars is... {was originally S4 in here}

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:19.110
Eternal!

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:25.490
Girls, I found an album of Yume for us.

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:27.450
Um, what are you doing?

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:35.120
I haven't flipped through this in forever.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:37.670
Looks like you've barely changed.

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:40.710
What? I'm much more grown up now.

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:44.920
Is this from when we opened the shop?

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:47.720
Yes, that really brings back memories.

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:51.680
You probably don't remember, but we couldn't have opened up without you.{this reminds me of furukawa pan}

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:52.470
Huh?

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:55.980
Hey, we've got a customer.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.980
Oh, Reina-chan. Welcome.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.230
Did you come here by yourself?

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:03.480
I-I have a favor to ask!

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.240
What is it?

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:11.240
Please make a cake with me!

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:27.840
A birthday cake, huh.

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:31.850
Yeah. I want to bake a cake for Mommy.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:37.480
But I don't know how...

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:39.980
Please help me!

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:41.610
Can we?

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:45.230
We're pretty backed up on orders today.

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:48.200
I'll do everything you tell me to!

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:50.990
So please...

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:54.240
I'll help her.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.500
Yume-chan! You're back?

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.000
Yep!

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.130
My friends are here too.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.760
It's Rola-chan and Ako-chan and Mahiru-chan!

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:09.010
Wow, wow!

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:12.640
So can we? Consider it my request too.

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:14.640
Yume-chan...

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:17.060
We'll help her too.

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:18.140
Yeah.

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:22.150
All right, you got it.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:24.770
Let's bake it together.

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:25.980
Yay!

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:32.990
Could you tell me some things your mom likes?

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:36.410
Um, she likes custard cream...

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.040
And grapes too!

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:44.590
Grapes are in season right now, so that works out great.

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:48.460
And also...

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:53.550
Flowers! She really likes her flower patterned one-piece dress.{so there should be a hyphen between "flower" and "patterned" but I don't like how it makes the line split move so we're not going to put one there}

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:58.560
That sounds beautiful. Let's make this something your mom will love.

00:15:58.970 --> 00:15:59.890
Yeah!

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:03.810
All right, firstly...

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:05.810
These!

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:09.320
We nabbed yummy-looking grapes.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:10.530
Nice!

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.570
And next...

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:15.620
Thank you very much.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:16.910
Thanks.

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:20.330
Oh!

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:27.710
There's one more place I want to swing by, 
so could you two head back first?

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:29.050
Are you sure?

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:30.510
Where are you going?

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:31.340
That's a secret!

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.970
You've got good technique.

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:39.260
I'd be ashamed if I didn't.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:40.220
There.

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:41.730
Perfect.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:44.980
Just one?!

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:48.650
A moment, Mahiru. How long are you planning to take?

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:52.990
It bothers me if I don't crack the shell perfectly.

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:56.490
Just look at how clean the split is.

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:59.660
J-Just how particular can you be?

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:03.000
I'm back!

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:08.880
We've got all our ingredients. Let's get baking!

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:10.500
Yeah!

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:28.980
Is that a friend?

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:31.650
Yeah, it's from Yume-chan. Look.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:33.280
Oh, Yume-chan.

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:35.200
She's really grown.

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:37.280
Are the other girls your friends too?

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:41.910
Yeah. They're all my dear Aikatsu buddies.

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:44.540
Done!

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:45.910
Awesome!

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:48.170
It's finally complete.

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:50.170
Hold your horses!

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:55.300
Actually, we haven't quite put the finishing touches on it yet.

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.470
Finishing touches?

00:17:56.470 --> 00:18:00.470
I would like to give the honor of doing it to Reina-chan.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:05.680
Reina-chan?

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:10.190
I'm sorry, but... I don't need the cake after all.

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:14.480
What do you mean you don't need it?

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:16.450
Is there something you don't like?

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:21.450
N-No, that's not it! It's just...

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:24.200
I'm in a fight with Mommy.

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:25.700
A fight?

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:32.460
Ever since my little brother was born, she stopped playing with me.

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:35.960
And then I said something selfish.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:41.220
I thought that baking her a cake would make her happy,

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:43.970
and then it'd be easier to say sorry.

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:47.230
But I'm just not brave enough.

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:50.230
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:55.280
Still, you want to celebrate your mom's birthday, right?

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:56.570
Yeah.

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:59.740
Then there's nothing to be afraid of.

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:06.240
If you show her how much you love her,
 I'm sure she'll understand.

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:11.370
She's right. Honesty is always the best policy.

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:13.250
This coming from you?

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:15.550
Just let me say my line here.

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:19.300
Reina-chan, don't you love her?

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:23.680
If you truly love her, you need to let her know.

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:28.980
We're all on your side.

00:19:31.390 --> 00:19:34.560
Why do you all care so much?

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:40.320
Because we want to see you smile, I think.

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:46.990
Besides, seeing someone you care about smile makes you happy yourself.

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:51.960
We want you to understand that too.

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:55.340
All that's left are the finishing touches.

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:57.590
Can we count on you?

00:19:58.420 --> 00:19:59.260
Yeah!

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:03.220
Oh, that's looking good!

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:06.220
Yume-chan, these flowers...

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:15.060
Yep, it's because you told me about your mom's flower-patterned one-piece.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:20.190
Aha. So this is what you went out to buy earlier.

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:21.280
I like it.

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:24.870
Yume-chan, everyone...

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:29.200
Thanks... thanks so much!

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:33.250
Goodbye!{I think we used "good-bye" at least once by the way}

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:35.040
Bye-bye!

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:36.250
See you!

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:37.250
Take care!

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:41.260
I'm glad Reina-chan was able to think positively again.

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:45.510
She might not have if not for all of your kindness.

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:47.510
Come to think of it,

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:51.770
what was the whole thing about not being able to open the shop without me?

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:54.770
Uh, you told her about that?

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:57.020
Sorry, it just slipped out.

00:20:57.020 --> 00:21:00.530
Well, it's really nothing special.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:03.820
Opening Soon

00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:03.820
We're supposed to open any day now,

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:06.490
but I still can't nail down a specialty menu.

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:08.280
What am I supposed to do?

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:14.330
Didn't I tell you to stay out of here?

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:16.330
Upsy-daisy.

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:19.000
That's a good girl.

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:23.340
Hey, wait!

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:24.720
Stop touch—

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:32.310
Daddy's sweets are so yummy!

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:39.520
It came to me when I saw your smile.

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:43.110
Pastries have the power to make people smile. {I thought they were medicine of the heart?}

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:46.490
And those are the kind of pastries I should make.

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:50.120
Your smile helped me move forward.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:51.990
Dad...

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:54.790
Pastries that make people smile.

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:56.120
That sounds just like...

00:21:56.120 --> 00:21:58.000
What an idol is supposed to do.

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:01.460
Yeah, I felt the same after watching you all today.

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:05.720
